The same Linux on the TCG model, booted on the development host by
`toyos-t14linux/tcg.sh` at commit 44eb3c2e (pull request #601) as

  qemu-system-x86_64 -nodefaults -machine q35
    -cpu qemu64,+rdrand,+smap,+fsgsbase,+x2apic,+smep -smp 2 -m 4G
    -kernel vmlinuz-6.8.0-142-generic -initrd s0.cpio
    -append "console=ttyS0 panic=-1" -serial stdio -display none -no-reboot

The kernel is the T14's /boot/vmlinuz-6.8.0-142-generic, and s0.cpio is the
T14's busybox with an init that mounts sysfs and proc, prints /proc/version and
`grep .` over /sys/devices/system/cpu/vulnerabilities/*, and powers off. Both
came off the T14 in the run that took ../t14/, and neither is committed.

  console.txt   the serial port, CRLF as it arrived
